{"translation": "But in the activities of this [breathing], while the need is being fulfilled but the animal is being worn out by the pains, choice once again takes away from the size, the speed and the frequency, at one time more from one, at another time more from another, as though it were at a loss [807] and neither able to stop the activity, for fear of suffocation, nor finding any cure for the pain. At any rate it passes at one time to one thing and at another time to another: to the one as something that will fulfil the need, to the other as something that will soothe the pain. And since, of all these, those that fulfil the need exacerbate the pains, while those that relieve these increase the need, and no remedy common to both is found, it passes in many ways to all of them through perplexity, always dissatisfied with what is present. And from this arises both the irregularity in each breath taken by itself and in all the breaths in succession, and the manifold disorder. For in the destruction of equality lies the genesis of all the irregularities and of the disorders. For this too was shown in the work on the differences of pulses: that consecutive equality is regularity, while periodic equality is order; and that when consecutive equality is destroyed, irregularity arises, and when periodic equality is destroyed, disorder.", "renderings": [{"target_no": 12, "surface": "ἀλγήμασι", "english": "pains", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 42, "surface": "πνίξεως,", "english": "suffocation", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 105, "surface": "καταμόνας", "english": "taken by itself", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 121, "surface": "ἰσότητος", "english": "equality", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 122, "surface": "διαφθορᾷ", "english": "destruction", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 125, "surface": "ἀνωμαλιῶν", "english": "irregularities", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 140, "surface": "σφυγμῶν,", "english": "pulses", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 146, "surface": "ὁμαλότης", "english": "regularity", "uncertain": "n"}], "uncertain_greek": ["ἑκάστῳ (masculine/neuter dative beside feminine ἀναπνοαῖς; perhaps read ἑκάστῃ)", "πολυει δῶς (split in Kühn; read πολυειδῶς)", "προαίρεσις (rendered 'choice')"]}
